WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.550
&gt;&gt;David Roberts: Mental Health Taskforce report
and its implementation.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:14.220
This is, I think, Bruce, information for the
Board on how we are thinking about taking

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.260
this subject forward, so perhaps again you
would care to give us a brief overview.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.270
&gt;&gt;Bruce Keogh: Thank you.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.230
I will be brief, Chair.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:30.280
It is clear that the NHS needs to improve
its offer to people with mental health problems,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:35.440
and I think I would like to reiterate Simon
Stevens's thanks to Paul Farmer and Jacqui

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:41.500
Dyer for the work that they did on the cancer
taskforce, which led to a recent publication

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.950
in the last ten days or so.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:55.700
What is clear to me is that there is a difference
in the way that we approach mental health

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:01.510
to the way we approach physical health, or
mental illness and physical illness.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:08.250
There are deep seated structural, cultural
and clinical differences.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:15.040
So the taskforce report aims to try and get
underneath some of those, but the point that

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.590
I would like to make is that this will not
be easy.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.000
It will be very difficult.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.890
I will come back to that in a second.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:30.710
The recommendations out of the report broadly
fall into three main areas.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:39.310
One is to provide a better seven-day service
for people with mental health crisis, and

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:47.049
in particular a focus on a liaison mental
health crisis resolution and so forth.

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:55.560
Secondly, to try and bring together the way
we look at mental health and physical health.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:02.200
There are many examples, really, of where
the two have an adverse synergistic effect

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.200
on each other.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:09.980
Then the third area is how we promote good
mental health, both in the workplace, for

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:14.450
offenders and for ordinary people.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:20.980
I think those are three very important areas,
but I will go back to my remark about the

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:27.970
deep seated structural, clinical and cultural
differences to say that they are sufficiently

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:31.050
deep seated, and people have tried to tackle
these issues before.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:37.670
I think it is going to be very important for
us in our governance processes - and the governance

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:44.330
structure is outlined on page 5 of the paper
- to understand what progress we are making,

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:48.740
how fast we are making it and where we are
making it, and also to understand what other

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:52.150
parts of the system might be inhibiting that
process.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.670
Dealing with mental health is not just an
issue of the NHS.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:03:02.680
It is an issue of work that is done by DWP,
it is an issue of housing, it is an issue

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:07.400
of veterans' health, it is an issue of offender
health and so forth.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.670
It is a complex issue.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:16.019
You will notice that attached to the paper
are a number of recommendations which come

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:17.230
out of the report.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:27.840
I think the lion's share falls to NHS England,
but many recommendations also fall to other

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:35.780
jurisdictions in Government, and Jeremy Heywood
is fixing up a group to oversee how those

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.629
particular areas might be tackled.

00:03:37.629 --> 00:03:39.769
&gt;&gt;David Roberts: Okay, good.

00:03:39.769 --> 00:03:41.370
Jane, any comments?

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:45.459
&gt;&gt;Jane Cummings: I am just welcoming the report.

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:49.880
What has been really helpful from my point
of view is the synergy and the link between

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.360
so many other of our national priorities.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:04:00.440
As Simon said earlier, we published the maternity
review earlier this week, on Tuesday, and

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.489
actually if you look at that the emphasis
on perinatal mental health is an absolute

00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:05.489
priority.

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:09.810
It is really helpful to see that it is also
one of the key recommendations in this.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:14.959
You can see that there is a general view about
what is the right thing to do, and that has

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:15.959
been really important.

00:04:15.959 --> 00:04:22.079
The other area for me, when you look at our
national priorities, is the support in here

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:28.270
for 24 hour crisis support, which is absolutely
essential in managing urgent and emergency

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.560
care.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.210
There is a synergy between this and the work
we are doing on learning disability around

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:40.150
physical health and things like employment,
both of which are really important for people's

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:43.710
mental health, but also direct links with
the other work that we are leading.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:48.729
So I absolutely welcome it, and look forward
to supporting Bruce in its implementation.

00:04:48.729 --> 00:04:55.570
&gt;&gt;Bruce Keogh: Chairman, may I please just
add to what Jane has said?

00:04:55.570 --> 00:05:01.860
We also want to see that we look at many of
our other clinical priorities through a mental-health

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:02.860
lens.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:10.870
So, for example, when we look at how we stress-test
our implementation of the urgent and emergency

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:18.960
care review, one of the areas that we include
in that is mental health, along with some

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.340
other cohorts of patients.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:28.660
Secondly, we will also include it, of course,
in the implementation and deliberations which

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.220
surround the cancer taskforce implementation.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:33.220
&gt;&gt;David Roberts: Okay, questions.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.220
Victor?

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:40.360
&gt;&gt;Victor Adebowale: Just one, really: how
and when are we going to measure progress?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:45.860
&gt;&gt;Bruce Keogh: I think that is something that
we are going to have to discuss at the implementation

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:52.770
board, but I would suggest that the Board
might want to decide the timeframe regularity

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.610
at which we bring reports back to this Board.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:58.949
&gt;&gt;Jane Cummings: Can I add to that?

00:05:58.949 --> 00:06:06.460
Clearly we are working very closely with the
team and the taskforce team.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:13.460
We are working through a plan for how the
recommendations will be taken forward into

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:14.460
implementation.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:26.480
That is one of our ten priorities for next
year for NHS England, and we already are working

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:32.900
out what the key aspects are that we will
need to implement during 2016.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:38.889
In fact, we are working on a three-year programme
of implementation so that we can see what

00:06:38.889 --> 00:06:44.449
happens next year and the following three
years.

00:06:44.449 --> 00:06:53.020
That plan will be part of our business plan,
and our business plan will be published at

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:58.860
the end of the year and agreed through this
Board on 31st March.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:04.319
Just so that you are aware and we are all
aware, that we will be looking to track progress

00:07:04.319 --> 00:07:13.110
and report progress to this Board on both
that one-year plan and looking forward across

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.830
the three-year plan.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.860
The three-year plan obviously needs to support
and align with the Five-Year Forward View

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:25.970
implementation and the work that is being
done on sustainability and transformation

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:29.440
plans in local areas as well.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.660
That is how we are planning to track and manage
delivery.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:42.630
&gt;&gt;David Roberts: I think, Victor, maybe if
I could put words into your mouth, given how

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:48.910
challenging this area and this subject has
been in terms of making demonstrable progress

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:55.180
on the ground, and given the catastrophic
impact on people's lives and actually in the

00:07:55.180 --> 00:08:00.610
economy more broadly, because of the cost
of mental illnesses, stress-related illnesses

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:08.440
and so on, whilst it is for Malcolm to decide,
I certainly wonder whether we should have

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:15.289
a particular focus on this on a more regular
basis than we might otherwise do, because

00:08:15.289 --> 00:08:21.150
it has been historically such a challenging
area in the Health Service to make real, demonstrable

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:22.150
progress on.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:28.970
&gt;&gt;Victor Adebowale: Yes, those were the words
that I was going to pull out of my mouth.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:31.809
We are just like puppet and master.

00:08:31.809 --> 00:08:35.729
I think there is a couple of things.

00:08:35.729 --> 00:08:41.010
First of all, it is true that what gets measured
gets managed, and I would not want the excellent

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.500
to get in the way of the good enough.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.830
There are some leading indicators; there are
some people who have a far worse experience

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.850
of the mental health service than others,
so that is a clue.

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:52.950
Perhaps we should start there, in terms of
the outcomes.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:58.100
My view is that we should be seeing something
quarterly, and we should see something back

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:05.950
from the taskforce as to what that dashboard
is going to look like in the autumn.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:12.120
So we get the dashboard, and then we get something
to the Board on a quarterly basis, because

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.420
we have been here before.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.730
The difference has to be that we actually
measure progress this time.

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:19.959
&gt;&gt;David Roberts: Okay.

00:09:19.959 --> 00:09:23.470
I will feed that back to Malcolm, as well.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:25.959
Ian, you are wanting to add something.

00:09:25.959 --> 00:09:32.270
&gt;&gt;Ian Dodge: I just wanted to add, partly
to provide some reassurance, three things.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:39.750
One is the new CCG improvement and assessment
framework - which we have developed with lots

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:44.880
of stakeholders, including Paul Farmer and
our mental health colleagues - will include

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.399
within it a suite of indicators in relation
to mental health.

00:09:49.399 --> 00:09:51.459
&gt;&gt;Victor Adebowale: That is reassuring.

00:09:51.459 --> 00:09:57.170
&gt;&gt;Ian Dodge: Our intention is that that then
forms the basis of what will be updated reporting

00:09:57.170 --> 00:10:04.399
arrangements into the Commissioning Committee
around system performance.

00:10:04.399 --> 00:10:12.060
Our aspiration is to provide clarity to all
CCGs and, ideally, aggregated to the 44 transformation

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:19.060
footprint areas supporting SDPs, the baseline
data on those metrics.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:25.399
We are aiming to do that within the next couple
of months if we can.

00:10:25.399 --> 00:10:32.820
Additionally, as part of the new CCG improvement
and assessment framework, there will be six

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:40.620
clinical priority areas where there will be
a single aggregate score on performance, and

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:44.350
one of those areas will be mental health.

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:49.470
Paul Farmer has agreed to chair, in essence,
a moderation panel to provide some independent

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:57.690
assurance on the overall performance in different
geographies around performance on mental health.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:05.140
Then thirdly, I just wanted to pick up on
Karen's point around sustainability and transformation

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:13.130
plans, because we have a process for the NHS
to come back with clarity about how it is

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:22.450
going to deal with the gap between the baseline
position and ambitions for where each locality

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:25.760
will get to by 2020-21.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:33.320
They will be submitting their plans for formal
assessment by the end of June, and therefore

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:40.740
we will in July have a clear sense of what
concrete plans are in place to measure progress

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.950
on mental health through that process.

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:51.260
&gt;&gt;Victor Adebowale: I chaired a parity of
esteem group some time ago.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.010
What is happening to that?

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:58.470
Is that merged into this, or is it something
that continues separately?

00:11:58.470 --> 00:11:59.470
I would hate to think it was layered.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:03.420
&gt;&gt;Jane Cummings: As I understand it, it is
wrapped into this new governance structure,

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:08.620
so that we have a single governance structure
that links to the Five-Year Forward View but

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:13.100
absolutely takes responsibility for all the
work of the taskforce and delivery of the

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.139
taskforce.

00:12:14.139 --> 00:12:19.700
The advisory board, which will be chaired
by Paul Farmer, feeds in as part of that process

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:23.480
to make sure that the programme is delivering
the intent of the taskforce.

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:24.540
&gt;&gt;Victor Adebowale: Very good.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.399
&gt;&gt;Richard Barker: Perhaps I could respond
further?

00:12:26.399 --> 00:12:30.390
Right in the here and now, we are in the middle
of the operational planning round for 2016-17,

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:35.210
and on parity of esteem we are looking for
every CCG to demonstrate as a minimum that

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:38.800
they have invested the same amount of new
money in mental health and learning disability

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.540
services as they have invested in other services.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:43.920
That is already a planning criterion in the
short term.

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:47.519
Also, just in the next year, in anticipation
of this report - obviously we could not anticipate

00:12:47.519 --> 00:12:51.470
everything - we are introducing some new commitment
around early intervention in psychosis and

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:54.050
some waiting time targets around psychological
therapies.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:58.550
Clearly there is a lot more to do, as signified
by the report, but we are trying to get ahead

00:12:58.550 --> 00:12:59.930
of that in the operational planning round
to make some early changes.

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:04.190
&gt;&gt;John Burn: Briefly, Chair, can I just ask
about training existing staff?

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:13.029
The situation is a lot easier than it has
been in the past, in the sense that we have

00:13:13.029 --> 00:13:17.290
got high-profile media people declaring themselves
to have mental illness, we have got lots of

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:20.209
media coverage from BBC programmes and so
on.

00:13:20.209 --> 00:13:24.889
Nevertheless, it is still a big stigma, and
one of the issues that is often forgotten

00:13:24.889 --> 00:13:29.410
is that people with mental health die of physical
diseases that they do not need to die of,

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:31.770
such as cancer, heart disease and smoking-related
conditions.

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:36.930
So, in a sense, we need to be thinking about
the whole workforce - and rather the same

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:40.980
with the learning disabilities - to get their
level of awareness up that these people are

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:42.830
harder to get to.

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:46.399
How do we get round that resistance to treatment?

00:13:46.399 --> 00:13:48.639
Is that something that is on your radar?

00:13:48.639 --> 00:13:50.610
&gt;&gt;Jane Cummings: Yes, absolutely.

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:56.850
Health Education England have got some quite
detailed plans that they are developing, particularly

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:00.570
looking at learning disability and mental
health.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:07.510
If they were here, Lisa, the director of nursing
in HEE, would say that there is a layered

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:12.310
approach where they are raising awareness
and then doing more detailed work, depending

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:15.240
on what roles people have.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:19.600
Some of that might be about online training,
which is much easier for people to access

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:25.709
and do, but we know from the work I have been
leading in learning disability that the impact

00:14:25.709 --> 00:14:31.199
of poor physical health means that people
do die a lot earlier, and we have exactly

00:14:31.199 --> 00:14:33.399
the same issue with people with mental health
issues.

00:14:33.399 --> 00:14:38.670
So they are working, and they are part of
the teams that are looking at this in the

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:39.670
round.

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:43.430
So, Health Education England working alongside
us to make sure that the outcomes are right,

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:46.699
and that the education is appropriate for
the needs of the patients.

00:14:46.699 --> 00:14:47.740
&gt;&gt;David Roberts: Okay.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:51.459
Simon, anything you want to add to this conversation?

00:14:51.459 --> 00:14:57.329
&gt;&gt;Simon Stevens: I think, practically speaking,
the two key deliverables that the mental health

00:14:57.329 --> 00:15:02.350
sector is already committed to doing in 2016-17
are the new waiting time standards for early

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:04.610
intervention psychosis services and IAPT.

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:12.420
Then, over and above that, we have been set
an affordable and impactful to-do list by

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:15.800
the taskforce in the areas that have already
been described.

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:21.680
We have to get the phasing of that right over
the next four years, but that is going to

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:25.990
be strongly supported if we can have much
greater transparency about what is going on

00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:31.579
inside the black box called the mental health
system, including funding flows, levels of

00:15:31.579 --> 00:15:35.480
activity and the clinical effectiveness of
the work that is being done.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:40.800
On all of those counts, frankly, part of the
reason why users of mental health services

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:45.200
have missed out is because there has not been
as much of that going on as there has been

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.300
in the rest of the healthcare system.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:48.890
&gt;&gt;David Roberts: Okay.

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:55.980
Paul, I am glad Simon said 'affordable', because
my question was going to be about money and

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:57.399
resources.

00:15:57.399 --> 00:16:02.630
Clearly we have a business plan conversation
to come, but can you give assurance to a reasonable

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:04.970
degree that this is in a good place?

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:05.970
&gt;&gt;Paul Baumann: Yes.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.329
The funding came in various forms.

00:16:07.329 --> 00:16:09.140
In fact, it has come in various stages.

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:14.670
The spending review (SR) was the final part
of that, or the main part of that, but we

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:19.300
have the funding to do the things which we
are committed to do in the taskforce.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:20.649
&gt;&gt;David Roberts: Good.

00:16:20.649 --> 00:16:21.550
Thank you.

